# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values: `cp .env.example .env`.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real tokens. It's an optional
# convenience for local runs of the integration suite (`go test
# ./integration/`); real environment variables always take precedence over
# it. See DEVELOPMENT.md's "Sacrificial Repository" section for full detail.

# Required to run the integration suite at all. Must point to a GitHub repo
# URL containing a `.git-sd-test-marker` file at its root (a safety check
# against running destructive test operations against the wrong repo). If
# unset, the suite skips cleanly (not a failure).
GIT_SD_TEST_REPO=https://github.com/<owner>/<sacrificial-repo>

# Optional. A GitHub token (PAT) used for every "author" action the suite
# performs (creating commits/PRs, syncing, merging, cleanup) — the account
# that owns/drives the sacrificial repo's test activity. If unset, author-side
# calls fall back to whatever account is logged into `gh` on the machine
# running the tests (`gh auth login`) — the original behavior before this
# variable existed.
#
# Get it: if that account already has an active `gh auth login` session on
# this machine, `gh auth token` prints its current token directly. Otherwise
# generate a PAT with the `repo` scope at https://github.com/settings/tokens.
GIT_SD_TEST_AUTHOR_TOKEN=

# Optional. A GitHub PAT for a SECOND, genuinely different GitHub account,
# used only to approve PRs the author created — GitHub forbids self-approval,
# so this is the only way to test "a PR gets approved by someone else, and
# merge actually completes" (TestSDMergeSucceedsWithSecondReviewerApproval).
# If unset, that one scenario skips cleanly; nothing else in the suite is
# affected.
#
# Setup: add the second account as a collaborator on the sacrificial repo
# (repo Settings -> Collaborators -> Add people; the invite must be accepted
# before it has any access), then generate a token for it — either a
# fine-grained PAT (https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta) scoped to
# just that repo with "Pull requests: Read and write", or a classic PAT
# (https://github.com/settings/tokens) with the `repo` scope.
GIT_SD_TEST_REVIEWER_TOKEN=
